@startuml
!theme plain
title v1.4 Authentication and Refresh Rotation
actor User
participant "Web BFF" as Web
participant "FastAPI Auth" as API
database "PostgreSQL\nlsa_auth" as DB
participant "Token Service" as Token

User -> Web: Submit institution, email, password, active role
Web -> API: POST /auth/login
API -> DB: Resolve institution
API -> DB: SET LOCAL app.tenant_id
API -> DB: Read user, membership, credential, role assignment
API -> API: Verify Argon2id and lockout state
API -> Token: Sign short-lived access token
API -> DB: Store hashed opaque refresh session
API --> Web: Access + refresh token pair
Web -> Web: Store both in HTTP-only SameSite cookies
Web --> User: Open unified work area

== Rotation ==
User -> Web: Authenticated request after access expiry
Web -> API: POST /auth/refresh with refresh cookie
API -> DB: SET LOCAL tenant from opaque token prefix
API -> DB: Lock and validate session hash, membership, role
API -> DB: Revoke old session; insert linked replacement
API -> Token: Sign new access token
API --> Web: Rotated token pair
Web -> Web: Replace HTTP-only cookies
@enduml
